      "message": "Thanks for working on this.\n\nNot asking to split the change at this stage.\n\nIn addition to inline comments:\n\n1) Duplication: get_crumb (3 copies), the secrets permission check (3), the proxy unset block (7), and the virsh teardown (3). Move them into one shared lib.\n2) Stale references:\n\n- central_deploy/students.yaml.example L13: the \"project\" comment refers to resolve_job_name() in setup_students.sh, which doesn\u0027t exist. The header comment (L5) also says existing \"jobs\" are skipped, but no jobs are created. Fix: describe \"project\" as a free-text label for the instructor\u0027s reference only, and drop \"jobs\" from L5.\n\n- central_deploy/reset_students.sh L2: says \"mock central Jenkins\". Fix: change to \"central Jenkins\".\n\n- student_deploy/secrets.yml.example L4-5: describes gerrit_owner_username as used by a \"Check-owner gating stage\", which no longer exists (routing is now by agent label). Fix: remove the field, or re-describe it (see \"Unused code\" below).\n\n- deploy_verify.sh L57 (register_gerrit_trigger comment): says GERRIT_CHANGE_OWNER_USERNAME is null, but the Jenkinsfile uses GERRIT_PATCHSET_UPLOADER_USERNAME. Fix: use the same variable name as the Jenkinsfile.\n\n- jobs/jenkins-dr-test/Jenkinsfile L69-71: the comment says submitter: doesn\u0027t block anyone under loggedInUsersCanDoAnything, but the authorization strategy is now globalMatrix. Fix: update the comment to match the current strategy and the actual behavior of submitter:.\n\n- central_deploy/gerrit_central.yml.example L3-4: says run.sh reads this file for its own Gerrit push, but run.sh now takes identities from scripts/gerrit_users.sh. Fix: state that this file is used only by deploy_central_jenkins.sh.\n\n3. Unused code:\n\n- central_deploy/roles/jenkins/templates/jenkins.yaml.j2 L8-12 (globalNodeProperties GERRIT_OWNER_USERNAME) and student_deploy/templates/jenkins-agent.service.j2 L7 (Environment\u003dGERRIT_OWNER_USERNAME):",
