      "side": 1,
      "message": "Problem: The first start happens with no plugins, so JCasC isn\u0027t applied and the authorization strategy is Unsecured. Anyone reaching :8080 is admin until plugins install and Jenkins restarts. Since the production deploy is a first boot by definition, this window always occurs. In addition, 00-admin-password.groovy recreates an admin user and replaces the realm on every boot.\nFix: Pre-install plugins with jenkins-plugin-cli --plugin-file plugins.txt into {{ jenkins_home }}/plugins before the first start. Then delete 00-admin-password.groovy, the jenkins-cli.jar download, and the post-install restart.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 223,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 240,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "3dffa0f9f3e5b2e39a13fd0a7d081baef3abfa7a",
