      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T05:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general, we have a stage of Jenkins deployment where admin-related config is specified. This step runs once for disaster recovery. Disaster recovery runs manually, and the script that runs must ask for a configuration (initial_setup_info.yaml or something similar, but not students.yaml) with admin credentials, port number, URL, etc. The same script must also run from CI, taking dummy credentials, port number, URL, etc., for the CI run.\n\nAnother stage: a script that deletes students and adds students every semester. The same script runs from CI and manually every semester (e.g., taking /students.yaml as a parameter for addition).\n \nA third stage is connecting student machines as agents. In CI, we simulate them as VMs. In real life, we again run the script manually. We want the same script to work in two modes (CI/manual) to keep things in one place (one mechanism, different parameters).",
      "revId": "3dffa0f9f3e5b2e39a13fd0a7d081baef3abfa7a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
